      {
        "tool_use_id": "call_92780ec5db6045de8830a5b5",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "     1→# Code Agent Daily\n     2→\n     3→A TypeScript-based product research daily report website focusing on the agentic coding area.\n     4→\n     5→[![](https://img.shields.io/badge/Build_with_GLM_Coding_Plan-5D6EFF)](https://www.bigmodel.cn/claude-code?ic=T3SS5DGX2N)\n     6→\n     7→## Live Demo\n     8→\n     9→Explore the generated reports index (latest 7 days): https://youfocal.com/\n    10→\n    11→\n    12→## Overview\n    13→\n    14→This project automatically discovers and tracks:\n    15→1. **New good products** in the agentic coding space\n    16→2. **Updates for whitelist products** - following changes to curated tools\n    17→3. **Topics about technical insights, ideas, and opinions** from well-known leaders\n    18→\n    19→## Features\n    20→\n    21→The project provides four main CLI commands for managing research reports:\n    22→\n    23→### 1. Auto-dated Update (Default)\n    24→```bash\n    25→yarn update\n    26→```\n    27→- Creates a workspace directory at `updates/{YYYY-MM-DD}/` (if it doesn't exist)\n    28→- Runs Claude Agent SDK workflow to research and generate reports\n    29→- Writes findings to disk in the workspace folder\n    30→\n    31→### 2. Custom Workspace Update\n    32→```bash\n    33→yarn update -- --workspace /tmp/2025-11-20\n    34→```\n    35→- Uses the specified directory as workspace root for Claude Agent SDK\n    36→- Creates the directory if it doesn't exist\n    37→- Generates and saves reports to the custom location\n    38→\n    39→### 3. List Mode (Read-only)\n    40→```bash\n    41→yarn update -- --list\n    42→```\n    43→- Runs the research workflow without writing files\n    44→- Displays content (title, description) to stdout only\n    45→- Useful for previewing what would be generated\n    46→\n    47→### 4. Quick Single Prompt Test\n    48→```bash\n    49→yarn task prompts/insights-prompt.md\n    50→```\n    51→- Runs just one prompt file and prints parsed JSON to stdout\n    52→- 